$t['Outgrown the Cage (small)'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: Outgrown the Cage - a small antique birdcage bursting at the seams as a much larger figure grows out between its bent bars. Tattoo style: black-and-grey realism. It is real tattoo art made for skin - tattoo linework, shading and colour the way a tattoo artist would ink it, not a photo or a painting pasted onto the body. The design has an open, organic shape that grows out of its own elements - no frame, no border, no oval or circle outline, no background panel behind it. No text, labels, logos or watermarks in the tattoo. In the right panel it is a small tattoo about the size of a palm, placed on the side of a woman''s ribs - a close-up photo of that spot so the small tattoo is sharp and easy to see. The design is simplified for its small size with clean, bold lines and sits naturally on the skin, following the curve of the body.'
$spent = 0.0
foreach ($k in $t.Keys) {
  $body = @{ subject=$t[$k]; model="gpt-image-2"; width=1536; height=1024; exact_size=$true; raw=$true } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress
  try { $j = (RUN ("SHOW_IT " + $body)) | ConvertFrom-Json
    if ($j.payload.ok -and $j.payload.id) { $spent += [double]$j.payload.cost_usd; "  " + $k + " -> " + $j.payload.image_url } else { "  " + $k + " -> NOT DRAWN: " + $j.payload.error } } catch { "  " + $k + " -> NOT DRAWN: " + $_.Exception.Message } }
$bn = 'A wide panoramic header banner for the "Freedom & Rebellion" category of a tattoo website. On the left, a close-up real photograph, framed close from the waist up so the person fills the full height of the photo and the tattoo is large, sharp and easy to read: a woman in her twenties with a shaved side cut, dark eyeliner and a nose ring, in a ripped black tank top, flexing her arm toward the camera with a defiant smirk in hard dramatic light. Her upper arm carries a black and red trash polka tattoo of a snapped chain and a cracked crown. On the right, on a gritty dark background of torn flyers and spray paint, the words "Freedom & Rebellion" written large in distressed red stencil spray-paint lettering, surrounded by rebel tattoo art - broken chains, a key snapped in half, a giant question mark smashing through paperwork, a lit match, a torn ID tag and an open birdcage. The art fades softly into the photo through drifting spray-paint mist. Raw, defiant and vivid, high detail. Only the words "Freedom & Rebellion", no other text, no watermark, no logos.'
$body = @{ subject=$bn; model="gpt-image-2"; width=2048; height=768; exact_size=$true; raw=$true } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress
try { $j = (RUN ("SHOW_IT " + $body)) | ConvertFrom-Json
  if ($j.payload.ok -and $j.payload.id) { $spent += [double]$j.payload.cost_usd; "  BANNER Freedom & Rebellion -> " + $j.payload.image_url } else { "  BANNER -> NOT DRAWN: " + $j.payload.error } } catch { "  BANNER -> NOT DRAWN: " + $_.Exception.Message }
